# Flavor Management Rules

## Flavor System Overview

The project uses three flavors managed by `flutter_flavorizr` and accessed through the `F` class.

### Supported Flavors

- **dev**: Development environment with debug features
- **stg**: Staging environment that mirrors production
- **prod**: Production environment for live deployment

## Flavor Class Usage

### Accessing Current Flavor

```dart
// Get current flavor enum
Flavor? currentFlavor = F.appFlavor;

// Get flavor name as string
String flavorName = F.name; // 'dev', 'stg', or 'prod'

// Get app title based on flavor
String appTitle = F.title; // 'Meup Dev', 'Meup Staging', or 'Meup'

// Get Firebase options for current flavor
FirebaseOptions firebaseOptions = F.firebaseOptions;
```

### Environment-Specific Logic

```dart
// Check specific flavor
bool isDevelopment = F.appFlavor == Flavor.dev;
bool isStaging = F.appFlavor == Flavor.stg;
bool isProduction = F.appFlavor == Flavor.prod;

// Environment-specific behavior using switch expressions
String get apiBaseUrl {
  return switch (F.appFlavor) {
    Flavor.dev => 'https://dev.venusshop.top/api/v1',
    Flavor.stg => 'https://dev.venusshop.top/api/v1',
    Flavor.prod => 'https://venusshop.top/api/v1',
    _ => 'https://venusshop.top/api/v1',
  };
}

bool get enableDebugFeatures {
  return switch (F.appFlavor) {
    Flavor.dev => true,
    Flavor.stg => false,
    Flavor.prod => false,
    _ => false,
  };
}

Duration get cacheTimeout {
  return switch (F.appFlavor) {
    Flavor.dev => const Duration(seconds: 30), // Short cache for dev
    Flavor.stg => const Duration(minutes: 5),  // Medium cache for staging
    Flavor.prod => const Duration(hours: 1),   // Long cache for production
    _ => const Duration(minutes: 5),
  };
}
```

## Entry Point Pattern

### Flavor-Specific Main Files

Each flavor has its own entry point that sets the flavor before calling common main:

```dart
// lib/main_dev.dart
import 'flavors.dart';
import 'main.dart' as runner;

void main() {
  F.appFlavor = Flavor.dev;
  runner.main();
}

// lib/main_stg.dart
import 'flavors.dart';
import 'main.dart' as runner;

void main() {
  F.appFlavor = Flavor.stg;
  runner.main();
}

// lib/main_prod.dart
import 'flavors.dart';
import 'main.dart' as runner;

void main() {
  F.appFlavor = Flavor.prod;
  runner.main();
}
```

### Common Main Implementation

```dart
// lib/main.dart
import 'package:meup/meup.dart';

void main() {
  AppService.instance.init(() => runApp(const AppProviders(child: DMainApp())));
}

class DMainApp extends StatelessWidget {
  const DMainApp({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return MaterialApp.router(
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,
      onGenerateTitle: (context) => context.l10n.appTitle,
      title: F.title, // Uses flavor-specific title
      // ... rest of app configuration
    );
  }
}
```

## Firebase Integration

### Flavor-Specific Firebase Configuration

```dart
// lib/flavors.dart
class F {
  static Flavor? appFlavor;

  static FirebaseOptions get firebaseOptions {
    return switch (appFlavor) {
      Flavor.dev => dev.DefaultFirebaseOptions.currentPlatform,
      Flavor.stg => stg.DefaultFirebaseOptions.currentPlatform,
      Flavor.prod => prod.DefaultFirebaseOptions.currentPlatform,
      _ => throw UnsupportedError('No Firebase options set for this flavor')
    };
  }
}
```

### Firebase Service Configuration

```dart
@lazySingleton
class FirebaseService {
  Future<void> initialize() async {
    await Firebase.initializeApp(
      options: F.firebaseOptions,
    );

    // Configure analytics based on flavor
    if (F.appFlavor != Flavor.dev) {
      await FirebaseAnalytics.instance.setAnalyticsCollectionEnabled(true);
    }

    // Configure crashlytics
    await FirebaseCrashlytics.instance.setCrashlyticsCollectionEnabled(
      F.appFlavor == Flavor.prod,
    );
  }
}
```

## Build Configuration

### Environment Files

- `.env/.env.dev` - Development configuration
- `.env/.env.stg` - Staging configuration
- `.env/.env.prod` - Production configuration

### Build Commands

```bash
# Development build
flutter build apk --flavor dev --dart-define-from-file=.env/.env.dev -t lib/main_dev.dart

# Staging build
flutter build appbundle --flavor stg --dart-define-from-file=.env/.env.stg -t lib/main_stg.dart

# Production build
flutter build appbundle --flavor prod --dart-define-from-file=.env/.env.prod -t lib/main_prod.dart
```

### Using Build Scripts (Recommended)

```bash
# Android APK builds
./tools/macos/build/build_apk.sh dev
./tools/macos/build/build_apk.sh stg
./tools/macos/build/build_apk.sh prod

# Android App Bundle builds
./tools/macos/build/build_appbundle.sh dev
./tools/macos/build/build_appbundle.sh stg
./tools/macos/build/build_appbundle.sh prod

# iOS builds
./tools/macos/build/build_ipa.sh dev
./tools/macos/build/build_ipa.sh stg
./tools/macos/build/build_ipa.sh prod
```

## Android Flavor Configuration

### Flavorizr Generated Configuration

The `android/app/flavorizr.gradle.kts` file is automatically generated:

```kotlin
android.apply {
    flavorDimensions("flavor-type")

    productFlavors {
        create("dev") {
            dimension = "flavor-type"
            applicationId = "com.eup.meup.dev"
            resValue(type = "string", name = "app_name", value = "Meup Dev")
            buildConfigField(type = "String", name = "API_BASE_URL", value = "\"https://dev.venusshop.top/api/v1\"")
        }
        create("stg") {
            dimension = "flavor-type"
            applicationId = "com.eup.meup.stg"
            resValue(type = "string", name = "app_name", value = "Meup Staging")
            buildConfigField(type = "String", name = "API_BASE_URL", value = "\"https://dev.venusshop.top/api/v1\"")
        }
        create("prod") {
            dimension = "flavor-type"
            applicationId = "com.eup.meup"
            resValue(type = "string", name = "app_name", value = "Meup")
            buildConfigField(type = "String", name = "API_BASE_URL", value = "\"https://venusshop.top/api/v1\"")
        }
    }
}
```

## Flavor-Specific Features

### Debug Features

```dart
class DebugFeatures {
  static Widget? get debugPanel {
    if (F.appFlavor != Flavor.dev) {
      return null;
    }

    return FloatingActionButton(
      onPressed: () => _showDebugMenu(),
      backgroundColor: Colors.red,
      child: const Icon(Icons.bug_report),
    );
  }

  static void _showDebugMenu() {
    // Show debug information
    showDialog(
      context: navigatorKey.currentContext!,
      builder: (context) => AlertDialog(
        title: const Text('Debug Info'),
        content: Column(
          mainAxisSize: MainAxisSize.min,
          children: [
            Text('Flavor: ${F.name}'),
            Text('App Title: ${F.title}'),
            Text('Firebase Project: ${F.firebaseOptions.projectId}'),
          ],
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

### Logging Configuration

```dart
@lazySingleton
class LoggingService {
  void initialize() {
    final logLevel = switch (F.appFlavor) {
      Flavor.dev => Level.ALL,
      Flavor.stg => Level.INFO,
      Flavor.prod => Level.WARNING,
      _ => Level.WARNING,
    };

    Logger.root.level = logLevel;
    Logger.root.onRecord.listen((record) {
      if (F.appFlavor == Flavor.dev) {
        print('${record.level.name}: ${record.time}: ${record.message}');
      }
    });
  }
}
```

### Network Configuration

```dart
@lazySingleton
class NetworkService {
  Dio createDio() {
    final dio = Dio();

    // Add interceptors based on flavor
    if (F.appFlavor == Flavor.dev) {
      dio.interceptors.add(LogInterceptor(
        requestBody: true,
        responseBody: true,
      ));
    }

    // Set base URL from flavor configuration
    dio.options.baseUrl = _getApiBaseUrl();

    return dio;
  }

  String _getApiBaseUrl() {
    return switch (F.appFlavor) {
      Flavor.dev => 'https://dev.venusshop.top/api/v1',
      Flavor.stg => 'https://dev.venusshop.top/api/v1',
      Flavor.prod => 'https://venusshop.top/api/v1',
      _ => 'https://venusshop.top/api/v1',
    };
  }
}
```

## Testing with Flavors

### Setting Flavor in Tests

```dart
group('Flavor-dependent behavior', () {
  setUp(() {
    // Set flavor for testing
    F.appFlavor = Flavor.dev;
  });

  test('should enable debug features in development', () {
    expect(DebugFeatures.debugPanel, isNotNull);
  });

  test('should use correct API URL for development', () {
    final service = NetworkService();
    expect(service.apiBaseUrl, equals('https://dev.venusshop.top/api/v1'));
  });
});

group('Production flavor behavior', () {
  setUp(() {
    F.appFlavor = Flavor.prod;
  });

  test('should disable debug features in production', () {
    expect(DebugFeatures.debugPanel, isNull);
  });

  test('should use production API URL', () {
    final service = NetworkService();
    expect(service.apiBaseUrl, equals('https://venusshop.top/api/v1'));
  });
});
```

## Flavor Generation

### Updating Flavors

After modifying `flavorizr.yaml`:

```bash
# Clean previous generation
flutter clean

# Regenerate flavors
dart run flutter_flavorizr

# Get dependencies
flutter pub get
```

